1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,550
Event studies and parallel trends — One coefficient for every year around treatment

2
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:08,950
With many periods, estimate one coefficient for each year relative to treatment. Year −1 is the reference and is set to zero.

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:15,950
Leads, the years before treatment, should hover around zero: treated and control units moved together before the policy.

4
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:22,950
Lags, the years after treatment, trace out how the effect builds up over time.

5
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:29,950
Caution: flat leads do not prove parallel trends. A small trend like this one passes the pre-test (Roth 2022).

6
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:35,950
If that trend continued after treatment, part of the estimated effect would be bias rather than policy.

7
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:41,950
Report the event study, then check how robust it is with Honest DiD bounds (Rambachan & Roth 2023).
